JAKARTA BEAN VALIDATION - CONSTRAINTS CHEAT SHEET
==================================================
Package: jakarta.validation.constraints  (Spring Boot 3.x)
         javax.validation.constraints    (Spring Boot 2.x)

Dependency needed in pom.xml:

    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-validation</artifactId>
    </dependency>


1. MOST IMPORTANT CONSTRAINTS
--------------------------------------------------

@NotNull
    Checks: value is not null (empty string is allowed)
    Works on: any type

@NotEmpty
    Checks: not null and not empty ("" or size 0)
    Works on: String, Collection, Map, array

@NotBlank
    Checks: not null, not empty, not only spaces
    Works on: String only

@Size(min, max)
    Checks: length/size is within range
    Works on: String, Collection, Map, array

@Min(value) / @Max(value)
    Checks: number is at least / at most the value
    Works on: Integer, Long, BigDecimal, etc.

@Positive / @PositiveOrZero
    Checks: number > 0 / number >= 0
    Works on: numbers

@Negative / @NegativeOrZero
    Checks: number < 0 / number <= 0
    Works on: numbers

@DecimalMin / @DecimalMax
    Checks: same as Min/Max but for decimals
    Works on: BigDecimal, String

@Digits(integer, fraction)
    Checks: number of digits allowed (good for prices)
    Works on: numbers

@Email
    Checks: valid email format
    Works on: String

@Pattern(regexp)
    Checks: matches a regular expression
    Works on: String

@Past / @PastOrPresent
    Checks: date is in the past
    Works on: date/time types

@Future / @FutureOrPresent
    Checks: date is in the future
    Works on: date/time types

@AssertTrue / @AssertFalse
    Checks: boolean must be true / false
    Works on: boolean

@Null
    Checks: must be null
    Works on: any type


2. NotNull vs NotEmpty vs NotBlank (most confused)
--------------------------------------------------

    Value      @NotNull    @NotEmpty    @NotBlank
    null       invalid     invalid      invalid
    ""         valid       invalid      invalid
    "   "      valid       valid        invalid
    "abc"      valid       valid        valid

For String fields like "name", use @NotBlank.


3. EXAMPLE: CategoryRequest DTO
--------------------------------------------------

package com.clicKart.category.dto;

import jakarta.validation.constraints.NotBlank;
import jakarta.validation.constraints.Size;
import lombok.Getter;
import lombok.NoArgsConstructor;
import lombok.Setter;

@Getter
@Setter
@NoArgsConstructor
public class CategoryRequest {

    @NotBlank(message = "Category name is required")
    @Size(max = 100, message = "Category name must be at most 100 characters")
    private String name;

    @Size(max = 500, message = "Description must be at most 500 characters")
    private String description;
}


4. EXAMPLES FOR AN E-COMMERCE APP
--------------------------------------------------

@NotBlank
@Size(max = 100)
